      "writtenOn": "2021-10-15T18:21:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The interrupt-generating bits in CONTROL_4 are clear-on-read *if the underlying condition has cleared.* If VCONN is still OC when you read CONTROL_4, VCONN_OC will still be set after you read it. So I have separate state for the register value and the value of the underlying condition. When I read the register, I clear the interrupt bits (as if the conditions had been clear) but then add back in any conditions that are still present.\n\nThe logic for the status register is similar.",
      "parentUuid": "8a658ec1_b903a26b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "cc3e62be12fbd5142c8efa53ef9847b6db005899",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
