      "writtenOn": "2021-10-15T18:21:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My rationale for doing it this way was to match the design of syv682x_emul_set_status, where all the bits are interrupt bits. I used the register value directly in that case just because it seemed like the easiest thing to do.\n\nI could give this function a different signature, as you suggest. I could also avoid passing in register values entirely. I could have 10 functions (for 10 conditions), or I could have one function with 10 bool params. Or I could define a struct of 10 bools and take that as an argument to one function. Of those options, I think the last one has the least objectionable interface.\n\nDo you have a preference? If you want me to change the interface to the status register, I\u0027d prefer to do that in a follow-up CL that gets every instance.",
      "parentUuid": "19bdbe41_c895bdea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 129,
        "startChar": 5,
